    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d753">

                <pb facs="0845" n="651" xml:id="pg651"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Department of the Army Files: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 753<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary of the Navy</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gates</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Assistant
                        Chief of Staff for Plans to the Commander in Chief, United States Fleet</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gardner</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-21">21 July 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>ComNavEu passes action UnderSeeNavs 212100 to CominCh and CNO for Rear Admiral
                    Matthias B. Gardner.</p>
                <p>Please see Joint Chiefs memorandum to State War Navy Coordinating Committee 17
                    July 1945<anchor n="1" xml:id="d753-f1"/> original of which was delivered to
                    Colonel Harrison Gerhardt at <hi rendition="#small-caps">Terminal</hi> on 17
                    July 1945. …<anchor n="2" xml:id="d753-f2"/> We<anchor n="3" xml:id="d753-f3"/>
                    feel you should vigorously support treatment of Kiel [Canal] recommended by
                    Joint Chiefs if question of Kiel cannot be avoided.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
